From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] aggregation: copy attribution no longer trusts client
 time

Adversarial review of 3daed66 (confirmed by probe): 'earliest' compared the
client-supplied observed_at as strings, so a copy sent with a backdated
timestamp, or with an offset that sorts earlier as text, displaced the
original and the conclusion formed again with a copier as the third agent.
With the system clock and second-resolution timestamps the tie also fell to
an order that let the copy win.

A copy group (same slot, same normalised text) is still one source; it is
now credited to the member whose producer already contributes other evidence
to this composition, so copying can never add an agent, whatever the
timestamps or arrival order; ties go to store arrival order.

tests/copied_roots.rs: + backdated (2020-01-01T00:00:00Z) and offset
(2026-10-24T00:00:01-23:59) copies; fails before, passes after. Goldens,
golden_scenarios, datapath pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
